    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/vltanh/lean4-moving-sofa",
        "note": "The formalization of Baek's optimality theorem for the ordinary problem, by the same maintainer, registered in Palomar as PALOMAR-2026-10-02-000008. Its library MovingSofaOptimality, at commit 1174c5c25c1c66b807e368446d6682e8d0276759, is copied unchanged into this repository, for Baek's theorem and the area of Gerver's sofa; the Challenge does not use it. Dean Cureton's MovingSofa and Ruifeng Cao's sofa-formal also formalize the ordinary problem; docs/prior-work.md compares them. The earlier formal statement of the ambidextrous conjecture is listed separately below.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/pull/6424",
        "note": "An earlier Lean formalization of the ambidextrous sofa conjecture, proposed by frvnkliu on 19 September 2026 in FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/MovingSofa.lean. At commit b5289b1114c76b2c8a99407580d0ebb3adbb9ea4, it defines ambidextrous sofas, their area supremum and Romik's exact area, and states ambidextrousSofaConstant_eq_romiksSofa_area as an open conjecture with a sorry proof. The lower-bound statement also has a sorry proof; supporting facts, including the unit-square example, cubic-root uniqueness and the comparison with the ordinary sofa constant, are proved. This is an earlier formal statement and partial development, not a proof of global optimality or uniqueness. The present repository supplies proofs of optimality and uniqueness and constructs the maximizing shape. The earlier statement was consulted for the prior-work comparison in docs/prior-work.md; its declarations are not imported by this project. The source is pinned at https://github.com/frvnkliu/formal-conjectures/blob/b5289b1114c76b2c8a99407580d0ebb3adbb9ea4/FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/MovingSofa.lean.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      }
